{"shortDescription":"Montreal, Quebec--(Newsfile Corp. - September 15, 2026) - Silver Acadia Exploration Inc. CSE:SLA (\"SLA\" or the \"Company\") is pleased to report the final assay results from its Phase 1 drill program, including additional high-grade silver-gold-zinc-lead mineralization at the Hachey Zone and broad co…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Montreal, Quebec--(Newsfile Corp. - September 15, 2026) - ",{"type":"b","children":["Silver Acadia Exploration Inc. ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CSE:SLA","text":"CSE:SLA"}}]}," (\"",{"type":"b","children":["SLA"]},"\" or the \"",{"type":"b","children":["Company"]},"\") is pleased to report the final assay results from its Phase 1 drill program, including additional high-grade silver-gold-zinc-lead mineralization at the Hachey Zone and broad copper-bearing intervals at the Millstream Zone on its flagship Nicholas-Denys Project."]},{"type":"p","children":["With Phase 1 drilling complete, Silver Acadia has integrated the results with its extensive historical database, core scanning, summer mapping and updated geological and structural interpretation. This work is defining targets focused on the approximately 3-kilometre-long mineralized corridor at Nicholas-Denys encompassing the Henry, Hachey and Shaft zones, while also highlighting mineralization elsewhere along the broader regional Rocky Brook-Millstream structural system (see figure 1)."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"",{"type":"i","children":["Our systematic approach to Nicholas-Denys has significantly improved our understanding of the mineralized zones and, importantly, their relationship with secondary structures. We believe this is revealing the potential for a district-scale mineralized system."]},"\" said Julien Davy, CEO of Silver Acadia. \"",{"type":"i","children":["Within our 3-kilometre Main Zone of Interest, our evolving interpretation points to multiple high-grade silver shoots within broader mineralized envelopes. Beyond this initial area of focus, mineralization at Pine Tree W and the copper-rich Millstream Zone demonstrates that the broader Rocky Brook-Millstream structural system remains prospective and significantly underexplored."]},"\""]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Final Phase 1 Drill Results"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The final Phase 1 results continue to demonstrate significant silver, gold, zinc and lead mineralization at the Hachey Zone, further supporting the Company's interpretation of a structurally controlled mineralized corridor characterized by broader mineralized envelopes hosting higher-grade shoots."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Company's approximately 3-kilometre-long Main Zone of Interest was initially defined as a priority exploration area encompassing the Henry, Hachey and Shaft zones, where historical work and recent drilling have identified a strong concentration of silver-rich mineralization. The boundaries of this area are not interpreted as limits to the broader mineralized system."]},{"type":"p","children":["Five additional holes tested the Millstream and Pine Tree W zones along the regional Rocky Brook-Millstream structural system (Figure 1). At Millstream, drilling intersected multiple broad intervals of copper mineralization, including near surface ",{"type":"b","children":["23.8 m grading 0.49% Cu, 11.4 m grading 0.77% Cu and 9.8 m grading 0.85% Cu and 0.48% Zn"]},". While the geological relationship between the copper-rich Millstream Zone and the Ag-Au-Zn-Pb mineralization occurring elsewhere along the structural system it is not yet fully understood, these results demonstrate that significant mineralization occurs beyond the currently defined 3-kilometre Main Zone of Interest and highlight the broader multi-commodity exploration potential of the Nicholas-Denys Project."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Highlight assay results:"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole ND26-004 - Hachey Zone"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["1.1 m @ 467 g/t Ag, 0.7 g/t Au, 3.04% Zn and 3.70% Pb (1.1 m @ "]},{"type":"i","children":[{"type":"b","children":["510 g/t AgEq)"]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole ND26-006 - Hachey Zone"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":["8.6 m @ 91.5 g/t Ag, 1.51 g/t Au, 4.26% Zn and 1.24% Pb"]},{"type":"*","children":["5.5 m @ 374 g/t Ag, 1.4 g/t Au, 2.50% Zn and 2.34% Pb (",{"type":"i","children":[{"type":"b","children":["5.5 m @ 469.8 g/t AgEq)"]}]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"i","children":[{"type":"b","children":["including 1.8 m @ 878.8 g/t Ag, 3.7 g/t Au, 5.88% Zn and 5.36% Pb (1.8 m @ 1 131 g/t Ag)"]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole BC26-001B - Pine Tree W"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":["1 m @ 2.52 g/t Au, 1.09% Zn and 1.27% Pb"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole BC26-002 - Millstream Zone"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["11.3 m @ 0.60% Cu"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"i","children":[{"type":"b","children":["including 0.4 m @ 4.65% Cu and 121 g/t Ag"]}]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["11.4 m @ 0.77% Cu"]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole BC26-003 - Millstream Zone"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["9.8 m @ 0.85% Cu and 0.48% Zn"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"i","children":["including 5.4 m @ 1.27% Cu, 0.3 g/t Au and 0.86% Zn"]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole BC26-004 - Millstream Zone"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["23.8 m @ 0.49% Cu"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"i","children":["including 4.8 m @ 1.23% Cu, 0.4 g/t Au"]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole BC26-005 - Millstream Zone"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":["7.7 m @ 0.43% Cu"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"i","children":["including 1.9 m @ 0.75% Cu, 0.12 g/t Au"]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Full details regarding the Phase 1 drill program were previously disclosed in the Company's ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://api.newsfilecorp.com/redirect/7nqD3ie3bQ","linkText":"April 1, 2026"}},", and ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://api.newsfilecorp.com/redirect/ejk2JHzLqA","linkText":"April 23, 2026"}},", press releases."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Millstream and Pine Tree W Zones"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Drilling at the Millstream and Pine Tree W zones began in February 2026. The program tested two distinct styles of mineralization within the broader Rocky Brook-Millstream structural system: (1) known Skarn-type magnetite-copper mineralization in the historic Beresford Mines area along the Main Break at Millstream, and (2) Ag-Zn-Pb mineralization along the Rocky Brook structure at Pine Tree W."]},{"type":"p","children":["Five (5) drill holes totaling 1,034 metres were completed between February and early March 2026. All 5 holes reached their intended target areas; however, one hole was terminated before fully testing its target due to poor ground conditions (BC26-001)."]},{"type":"p","children":["At Millstream Iron A Zone, drilling predominantly intersected indurated sedimentary rocks consisting of bluish wacke, ferruginous sediments, sandstone, conglomerate and oxidized iron formations within the skarn alteration aureole of the Nicholas-Denys intrusion. Sulphide mineralization consists predominantly of chalcopyrite and sphalerite and is generally associated with sericite-chlorite alteration within the iron formations and their wall rocks. Mineralization occurs as fine-grained disseminations, clusters, veinlets and massive sulphide veins ranging from several millimetres to several centimetres in thickness."]},{"type":"p","children":["At Pine Tree W, drilling intersected a strongly foliated sedimentary sequence of interbedded wacke and mudrock containing rare early quartz veins. The sequence is strongly deformed, folded, boudinaged, dismembered and transposed. Sulphide mineralization consists of pyrrhotite, pyrite, sphalerite, galena and arsenopyrite occurring as disseminations, clusters, aggregates, stockworks, veinlets and massive sulphide veins ranging from several millimetres to several centimetres in thickness."]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"tmx_newsfile:5a7609853094b-f211c59b40d80a9ff17374dd755576ec","source-width":1613,"source-height":1243,"bg-color":"#cfcbcb"}}},{"type":"p","children":["Figure 1: Location of the Hachey, Millstream Iron A and Pine Tree W zones where the 2026 phase 1 drilling program was completed."]},{"type":"p","children":["To view an enhanced version of this graphic, please visit:"]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"tmx_newsfile:5a7609853094b-f211c59b40d80a9ff17374dd755576ec","source-width":1613,"source-height":1243,"bg-color":"#cfcbcb"}}},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Table 1"]}," Details of the drill holes reported in this news release"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Project"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Drilled Hole ID"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Azimuth"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Dip"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":[" Final Depth (m) "]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Target"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"rowspan":7},"children":[{"type":"b","children":["Nicholas-Denys"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["ND26-004"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["200"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["-67"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["150.0"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"rowspan":3},"children":["Hachey and Pine T